Restore the Dhcp6Dxe driver veto

Reverts iPXE commit 5e06c866a ("[efi] Remove the Dhcp6Dxe driver veto").

That commit removed the veto on the premise that, since iPXE now calls
UnloadImage() at TPL_APPLICATION, it no longer triggers the edk2 bug at
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/issues/10506, where EfiDhcp6Stop() spins
waiting for an event that never fires.

The premise does not hold when the firmware itself PXE-booted over IPv6:
Dhcp6Dxe is already bound before iPXE loads, and iPXE hangs at "initialising
devices" instead of reaching its banner. Bisected to 5e06c866a, whose parent
8796d2fb0 boots normally.

Reproduced against OVMF 202608 with IPv4 PXE disabled
(-fw_cfg opt/org.tianocore/IPv4PXESupport,string=false), so the newest edk2
does not carry a fix, and upstream iPXE master has no commits touching
efi_veto.c since the removal.

Drop this patch once edk2#10506 is fixed or upstream restores the veto.

--- a/src/interface/efi/efi_veto.c
+++ b/src/interface/efi/efi_veto.c
@@ -480,6 +480,30 @@ efi_veto_vmware_uefipxebc ( EFI_DRIVER_BINDING_PROTOCOL *binding __unused,
 	return 1;
 }
 
+/**
+ * Veto Dhcp6Dxe driver
+ *
+ * @v binding		Driver binding protocol
+ * @v loaded		Loaded image protocol
+ * @v manufacturer	Manufacturer name, if present
+ * @v name		Driver name, if present
+ * @ret vetoed		Driver is to be vetoed
+ */
+static int efi_veto_dhcp6 ( EFI_DRIVER_BINDING_PROTOCOL *binding __unused,
+			    EFI_LOADED_IMAGE_PROTOCOL *loaded __unused,
+			    const char *manufacturer __unused,
+			    const CHAR16 *name ) {
+	static const CHAR16 dhcp6[] = L"DHCP6 Protocol Driver";
+
+	/* Check driver name */
+	if ( ! name )
+		return 0;
+	if ( memcmp ( name, dhcp6, sizeof ( dhcp6 ) ) != 0 )
+		return 0;
+
+	return 1;
+}
+
 /** Driver vetoes */
 static struct efi_veto_candidate efi_vetoes[] = {
 	{
@@ -494,6 +518,10 @@ static struct efi_veto_candidate efi_vetoes[] = {
 		.name = "VMware UefiPxeBc",
 		.veto = efi_veto_vmware_uefipxebc,
 	},
+	{
+		.name = "Dhcp6",
+		.veto = efi_veto_dhcp6,
+	},
 };
 
